## Department scoping (how data is filtered)

Always pass department via API; **never hardcode** dept names.

| Screen | API scope | Filter |
|--------|-----------|--------|
| New | — | Equipment/areas for **logged-in dept** only; save stores `initiating_department` |
| Engg Review | `scope=all` | All depts, `status=TO_ENGG_REVIEW` |
| Work Performed | `scope=all` | All depts, `status=TO_PART_B` |
| Verification | `scope=department&department_name=` | **Own** dept, `TO_VERIFY` |
| QA Approval | `scope=all` | All depts, `TO_QA` |
| Work Order Log | `scope=department` | **Own** dept, all statuses |
| Issuance Log | `scope=all&status=ISSUANCE` | All depts, `CLOSED` **or** `TO_QA` |

`ISSUANCE` is a **query alias** (not a DB status): means `CLOSED OR TO_QA`.

### Equipment vs Area (`asset_type`)

| | Equipment | Area |
|--|-----------|------|
| Stored as | `asset_type=Equipment` | `asset_type=Area` |
| Name fields | equipment master | area / location / section / manual name |
| After review | → `TO_PART_B` | → `TO_PART_B` (same) |
| Work Performed | No checklist | Dropdown **Interior** or **Exterior**; save requires `checklist_type` + checklist JSON |
| Checklist columns | — | `interior_checklist_json` / `exterior_checklist_json` + `*_done` |

Checkpoint lists live in `checklist/facility-checklist.items.ts` (C = 13 items, D = 8 items).

